 \begin{abstract}
-Detecting fraud in the vast databases of the insurance industry
-remains an ongoing challenge. Existing algorithms often flag
-numerous suspicious cases, resulting in time-consuming and costly
-investigations. To address this issue, we propose a novel,
-sequential, and multilayered algorithm that achieves a high level
-of accuracy while presenting a manageable number of cases for
-expert review. In this article, we evaluate the performance of our
-algorithm using real-world data, demonstrating its impressive
-accuracy of over 95\% and notable speed. This approach offers a
-significant advancement in fraud detection for the insurance
-sector.
- \end{abstract}
-
-
-\noindent{\bf Keywords:} Fraud Detection;
-Supervised/Unsupervised/Reinforcement Learning; Artificial
-Intelligence; Insurance Application; Multilayer Algorithms.
